WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.601 line:7%
 My name is Ben Abbott.

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:05.171 line:0%
I've been making blades since
I was about 13 years old.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:06.639 line:0%
I was born in
Worcester, England.

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:09.475
When I saw all the cool
armor, and weapons, and stuff,

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:11.944
I just decided to start
making it for myself.

00:00:12.044 --> 00:00:13.913 line:7%
 My name's Tom McGinnis.

00:00:13.979 --> 00:00:17.984 line:0%
I'm 73 years old, and
I love knife making.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.953
I made my first knife in 1958.

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:25.225
I'm an old duck, but
I'm gonna hang tough.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.260
WIL WILLIS: Ben,
Tom, congratulations.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.629
You've made it to the
"Forged in Fire" final.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.597
And now we're sending
you back to your home

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:37.603
forges to recreate an
iconic weapon from history,

00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:40.172
the khanda .

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:42.842
The khanda is a sword
that gained popularity

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.744
in medieval India
during the Gupta

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.847
period between 320 and 550 AD.

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:51.083
The word khanda is derived from
the Sanskrit word [sanskrit],,

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:54.988
meaning to break,
divide, cut, or destroy.

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:57.123
It's wide, thick,
straight blade was

00:00:57.223 --> 00:01:01.493
not only used for thrusting,
but also as a hacking weapon.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:04.397
When a Rajput warrior was
surrounded by the enemy,

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:06.632
he would pull out the
khanda and fight to the end

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:09.101
while swinging the
blade with both hands,

00:01:09.201 --> 00:01:11.704
taking down as many
enemies as he could

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:15.207
in an honorable last stand.

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:18.644
It has to be an
authentic, working replica

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.813
of that deadly weapon.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.715
 The mystery
weapon is a khanda.

00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:24.717
I think it's a
real doable blade.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.819
I believe I can produce one.

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:28.321
 Bladesmiths, good luck.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:35.895
BEN: So it's day one.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:37.463
My strategy going into
building this blade

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:39.332
is that I'm going to make
a couple of test blades.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.668
The most crucial part of this
build is whatever I have to do

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:42.902
to get it through the testing.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.170
I can make the prettiest
thing in the world.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.139
If it snaps in two,
I'm going to lose.

00:01:47.239 --> 00:01:48.508
I'm going to quench the sword.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.380
[cackling]

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.048
The quench went really well.

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:57.282
Very excited about that.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.684
Now I have to dive
into the handle.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:01.053
The handle is nothing like
I've ever seen before.

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:02.989
I lost 10 hours
working on this sword.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:04.890
Got to just finish
grinding the blade.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.559
I wrap the handle in leather.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:08.828
It'll bulk out the handle
and make it more comfortable

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:11.830
so that it really kind
of holds your hand snugly

00:02:11.897 --> 00:02:13.899
and feels really good.

00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:15.801
Holy cow.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:16.870
What a long journey.

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:22.174
TOM: It feels good
to be back home

00:02:22.274 --> 00:02:23.709
where I have my own equipment.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:26.846
Today I'm going to try and
get the shapes of the guard

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:29.114
and get the blade ground.

00:02:29.181 --> 00:02:31.484
The blade we had
to make is designed

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:36.289
for fighting double handed,
and it had a big D guard on it,

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:39.191
and I've never done that.

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:41.827
It's quite an awesome blade.

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:43.896
I got the blade ground.

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:47.199
Seems to be going real good,
and I'm going to try and get

00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:48.835
the handle all put together.

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:54.307
I'm going to ask God to
help me with this one.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:08.154
God answered my prayer.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:11.124
It's pretty straight if
it will just cool down.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:14.226
Now, I know this
blade's going to cut.

00:03:14.293 --> 00:03:16.128
It's ready for the judges.

00:03:16.228 --> 00:03:19.265
Ben is gonna contend
with a tough old dog.

00:03:23.268 --> 00:03:26.439
 Tom, Ben, welcome
back to the forge.

00:03:26.505 --> 00:03:28.675
We will now be putting
each of your weapons

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:31.043
through three tests.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.279
Doug?

00:03:33.345 --> 00:03:35.380
 Bladesmiths, this
is the kill test.

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.683
To test the lethality and
function of your weapon,

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.819
I will take your weapon and
deliver three vertical chops

00:03:40.919 --> 00:03:42.888
and then a slice.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:43.656
Ben, you're up.

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:44.190
You ready?

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.658
 I guess so.

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:47.193
 Let's do this.

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:48.194
BEN: I'm a little bit nervous.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:49.696
There's a lot of bones in there.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:55.067
But this sword is made to
cut, so let's see it cut.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:58.605
[music playing]

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.613
 Well, Ben, the damage
that your blade did cut

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:11.717
about six inches deep into
both shoulders and right

00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:13.318
through the spine.

00:04:13.385 --> 00:04:15.087
On the horizontal
slice, it pretty much

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.789
cut all the way through.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:19.325
It's got a good feel.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.894
This, sir, will kill.

00:04:21.994 --> 00:04:22.928
 Thank you.

00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:23.829
 Tom, it's your turn.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:24.497
You ready?

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:25.330
 I'm ready.

00:04:25.397 --> 00:04:27.567
I don't like losing at all.

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:29.268
I like to win.

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:32.037
In the kill test, I
think it's doable.

00:04:32.137 --> 00:04:34.941
I really do.

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:38.411
[music playing]

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.619
DOUG: Tom, you definitely
cut in about six inches

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:50.756
deep on the shoulders
and about eight inches

00:04:50.856 --> 00:04:51.857
into the spinal column.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:54.960
You cut halfway through
into the carcass.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:59.832
Also feels good in balance
with a downward vertical slice.

00:04:59.898 --> 00:05:03.302
There was a slight bend that's
happening to your blade,

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:05.838
but it will kill.

00:05:09.708 --> 00:05:11.510
Bladesmiths, this is
the sharpness test.

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:13.846
I will slash across
these bungee cords.

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:16.682
If your blade is sharp, it
should cut all the way through.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:19.852
If not, it may just push
it aside or bounce off.

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:20.586
Ben, you're up.

00:05:20.687 --> 00:05:21.820
Are you ready?

00:05:21.887 --> 00:05:23.989
 Sure.

00:05:24.056 --> 00:05:25.725
At this point, I'm nervous.

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:26.993
I don't know.

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:28.294
I don't know if I'm going
to cut through all of them,

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:29.729
or if I'm going to bounce off.

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:30.663
I have no idea.

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:41.474
[bleep]

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.876
 Well, Ben, your
sword started to cut.

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:48.514
It cut a little bit, but
it did not cut through.

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:52.217
It feels good on the slice.

00:05:52.284 --> 00:05:54.453
The handle is very
comfortable in the hand.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.622
Once again, it
didn't cut through,

00:05:56.689 --> 00:06:00.760
so it brings into
question the sharpness.

00:06:00.827 --> 00:06:01.660
Tom, it's your turn.

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:02.194
You ready?

00:06:02.294 --> 00:06:03.229
 I'm ready.

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:04.697
DOUG: Let's do this.

00:06:04.764 --> 00:06:06.699
TOM: I really feel comfortable
going into the test,

00:06:06.765 --> 00:06:09.868
and I know this
blade's going to cut.

00:06:09.935 --> 00:06:12.771
I'm ready.

00:06:12.838 --> 00:06:13.506
Oh.

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:20.246
DOUG: Well, Tom, it
did cut a little bit

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:21.380
into the bungee cord.

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:22.815
But then--
- Yeah.

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:24.283
 --as you can see, the
transference of energy went

00:06:24.383 --> 00:06:25.518
all the way back to the blade.

00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:27.319
It wasn't sharp
enough to cut through,

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:31.057
and it bent your
blade, which brings

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:33.526
to question the heat treatment
you did on your blade.

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:35.227
 Cut around corners now.

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:36.528
[laughter]

00:06:36.595 --> 00:06:37.963
 It'll cut around
corners this time, right?

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:43.469
But in this particular
case, it will not cut, sir.

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:45.704
 When you don't have your
hardening and tampering right

00:06:45.804 --> 00:06:49.008 line:0%
on a blade, you
don't have anything.

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:50.109
 Gentlemen, both
of your weapons

00:06:50.175 --> 00:06:51.611
failed in the sharpness test.

00:06:54.413 --> 00:06:56.916
Historically in
battle, blades bent.

00:06:56.982 --> 00:06:59.685
Tom, we'd like to give
you the opportunity

00:06:59.751 --> 00:07:01.586
to straighten your
blade so that you

00:07:01.686 --> 00:07:03.556
can continue with this fight.

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:07.126
However, we will be taking
that bend into consideration

00:07:07.192 --> 00:07:08.461
when it comes to final judging.

00:07:08.528 --> 00:07:09.895
 I understand.

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:14.533
I should have left thicker,
but I'm not a quitter.

00:07:14.599 --> 00:07:15.902
I'm going to fight to the end.

00:07:19.304 --> 00:07:21.674
 OK, Tom, you've
straightened your blade.

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:23.042
We can continue with testing.

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:28.647
 Gentlemen, this is
the strength test.

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:32.185
I'm going to take five chops
into these copper pipes

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:34.987
and see how far
through we can split.

00:07:35.054 --> 00:07:36.822
Ben, are you ready?

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:38.057
 Not at all.

00:07:38.124 --> 00:07:39.591 line:7%
Yes.

00:07:39.691 --> 00:07:42.928 line:0%
The last thing I would bring
to a plumbing job is a sword.

00:07:43.028 --> 00:07:47.032
So I'm just nervous that
the blade will break,

00:07:47.132 --> 00:07:51.003
just snap in two.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:54.874
[music playing]

00:08:02.314 --> 00:08:04.617
JUDGE: Wow.

00:08:04.684 --> 00:08:09.021
Ben, it's still one
piece, but barely.

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:14.793
And the dimensions of your guard
here on my hand are perfect.

00:08:14.893 --> 00:08:17.329
Your blade, it's
held up beautifully.

00:08:17.429 --> 00:08:18.163
Nicely done.

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:19.231
 Thank you.

00:08:19.298 --> 00:08:21.000
 So, Tom, your turn.

00:08:21.067 --> 00:08:21.634
 OK.

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:22.935
JUDGE: All right.

00:08:23.001 --> 00:08:25.437
TOM: I'm really nervous
about the pipe cut.

00:08:25.537 --> 00:08:27.673
I should have spent
more time on my blade,

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:29.908
because that's what
counts in the end.

00:08:29.975 --> 00:08:31.711
 Now, Tom, we do have
that bend in your blade,

00:08:31.777 --> 00:08:33.879
and we know that there's at
least a soft section in there.

00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:35.280
 Yeah.

00:08:35.347 --> 00:08:37.683
 So as I'm cutting, if I feel
that there's a point where it's

00:08:37.783 --> 00:08:40.085
unsafe, I'm just gonna stop.

00:08:40.152 --> 00:08:40.853
All right?

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.188
 OK.

00:08:42.255 --> 00:08:45.725
[music playing]

00:08:49.629 --> 00:08:52.164
 So, Tom, what happened is
we lost a piece of the guard

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:52.898
right there.

00:08:52.965 --> 00:08:54.132
 Yeah.

00:08:54.199 --> 00:08:55.367
JUDGE: With the broken
guard and the bend earlier,

00:08:55.433 --> 00:08:57.770
I feel it's unsafe to continue.

00:08:57.837 --> 00:09:00.406
All right, thank you, Tom.

00:09:00.506 --> 00:09:01.874
TOM: I'm disappointed.

00:09:01.941 --> 00:09:05.444
I know I can do better, but
that's what happens when

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:07.079
you don't use your time right.

00:09:10.716 --> 00:09:12.751
 Gentlemen, in just
five days you've

00:09:12.851 --> 00:09:16.088
both done an amazing amount
of work on your khandas.

00:09:16.155 --> 00:09:19.324
But in this arena, there can
only be one "Forged in Fire"

00:09:19.391 --> 00:09:20.059
champion.

00:09:23.962 --> 00:09:29.301
Ben, you are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:29.368 --> 00:09:33.171
Tom, unfortunately your
weapon did not make the cut.

00:09:33.271 --> 00:09:37.609 line:0%
 Tom, as I said before, your
attention to detail is spot on.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:40.446 line:0%
It's just that heat-treat
problem with that blade

00:09:40.546 --> 00:09:42.347 line:7%
bending the way it did.

00:09:42.448 --> 00:09:44.383
That's why we have
to let you go.

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:47.520
 Tom, please
surrender your weapon.

00:09:47.587 --> 00:09:50.989
TOM: Well, I got to meet
some real nice craftsmen.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:52.658
And I learned.

00:09:52.725 --> 00:09:55.294
Don't let your
age slow you down.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:57.262
You don't know how long you got.

00:09:57.362 --> 00:09:58.798
 Ben, congratulations.

00:09:58.898 --> 00:10:00.699
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:10:00.765 --> 00:10:03.836
and will be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:10:03.903 --> 00:10:04.536
Good job.

00:10:04.603 --> 00:10:05.738
 Thank you.

00:10:05.804 --> 00:10:07.672
 Most people get
guard sizes all wrong,

00:10:07.772 --> 00:10:10.910
and the khanda has a
deceptively small guard.

00:10:10.976 --> 00:10:12.644
You just hit it out of the park.

00:10:12.711 --> 00:10:14.112
 Thank you.

00:10:14.212 --> 00:10:15.814
It feels amazing to be the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:10:15.914 --> 00:10:19.018
It's a wonderful validation of
a long time of knife making.

00:10:19.118 --> 00:10:20.452
And I made new friends.

00:10:20.519 --> 00:10:23.122
I made 10 grand.

00:10:23.222 --> 00:10:25.291
What more could you ask for?

